  "notes": "Term-by-term sequence transcribed verbatim from the official 2025-2026 American Baptist College catalog, 'DEGREE AUDIT SHEET for ENTREPRENEURSHIP STUDIES MAJORS' (40 courses x 3 credits = 120 credits). The 2025-2026 catalog is used because the 2026-2027 catalog's 'DEGREE AUDIT SHEET for ENTREPRENEURIAL LEADERSHIP STUDIES MAJORS' prints only 39 courses (117 credit hours) against its own 120-hour program header — its Year Four Spring shows 4 rows instead of 5 — and is therefore inconsistent with the degree requirements; the 2025-2026 sheet's 40 courses match the 120-hour total. The 2025-2026 catalog's program-code list gives 'BAEL - BA in Entrepreneurial Leadership'; the audit sheet header reads 'ENTREPRENEURSHIP STUDIES MAJORS', so the major is recorded as 'Entrepreneurship Studies' (the 2026-2027 catalog renames the program 'Entrepreneurial Leadership Studies'). 'PST 3080 Field Ed I' expanded to 'Field Education I' per the requirements block ('PST 3080 Field Education I'). Sheet parentheticals '(NT 203)' and '(TH 207)' are prior course codes, omitted from titles. Concentration/minor (18 hours / 6 courses) chosen by the sophomore year; the Marketing concentration lists 7 courses for a 6-course requirement, so advisor-guided selection of 6 applies. Option-level prereqs inside the concentration lists (COM 3000 and COM 3060 require ENG 1010; BEH 4040 requires ECO 3010 Principles of Microeconomics) are carried in the choice_note text, not as machine prereqs. The catalog's course-description header states 'Prerequisite to all Bible Courses is BST 1010'; the sequence places BST 1010 first, so it is documented here rather than repeated as a machine prereq. All ABC courses are 3 credit hours; total_credits equals the sum of ALL semester course credits including choice slots. transfer_confidence is 'core_only': ABC is a private four-year college with no published TCCNS/articulation equivalencies for these courses, so tccns mirrors the local course code.",
